    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="0464" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg384"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Takahira.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-09-25"><hi rendition="#italic">September 25,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The pressure of public business attendant
                    upon the death of President McKinley has delayed until now an acknowledgment of
                    the telegram from the Japanese minister for foreign affairs (copy of which was
                    left by you at the Department), conveying an expression of His Imperial
                    Majesty’s sympathy in view of that sad event.</p>
                <p>I shall be obliged if you will assure his excellency, in the name of the
                    Government and people of the United States, as well as in the name of the family
                    of the late President, that this message of sympathy on the part of His Majesty
                    was received with sincere and grateful appreciation.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
